Title: Modular AI Assistant System High-Level Design Document

1. Introduction
    - Purpose of the document is to outline the proposed architecture and components necessary for building a scalable, efficient, robust, secure, reliable, flexible, maintainable modular AI assistant system that caters to various industries including eCommerce, healthcare, customer service etc.. 

2. System Goals & Requirements
    - Identify the primary functions and capabilities of a modular AI Assistant such as understanding natural language queries/instructions, processing them in real-time for decision making with minimal latency while maintaining user privacy constraints. Determine specific system goals (such as accuracy levels or response time) based on industry needs.
    - Incorporate end users' requirements and expectations to ensure the designed architecture meets their demands, such as voice recognition features in a virtual assistant for hands-free operation over various devices 

3. System Architecture Overview (High Level Design View)
   - Define three main modules: Natural Language Understanding Module, Decision Making Module and User Interface module with subsystems or components that each fulfill their respective roles to enable the seamless functioning of entire AI assistant system; 
     a. Natural Language Understanding (NLU) Submodule for processing user's input text/voice commands using techniques such as speech recognition, language model training and intent classification etc.;  
     b. Decision Making Module to take processed inputs from NLU sub-module through an appropriate API call to various backend systems responsible for providing contextual data like weather updates in case of travel plans or checking stock availability on eCommerce platforms; 
    c. User Interface (UI) Submodule comprising frontend components that enable real-time interaction between AI Assistant and users by integrating speech recognition/text input as well visualization elements to enhance user experience while maintaining privacy through secure channels, encrypt data at rest & in transit;
    - Integration of third party APIs (e.g., Google Maps for location services) that can be swapped or updated independently without affecting the main system's architecture 

4. Communication and Data Flow Diagram: System interactions diagram detail how each module communicates with other modules in real-time using asynchronous communication protocol like WebSocket API, RPC etc.; include data flow diagrams that illustrate information moving between different components of a modular AI assistant system for better understanding; 
     - Input from user’s device(e.g., voice recognition) → Natural Language Understanding Module (processes and interprets input language/commands using NLU algorithms, extract intents etc.) → Decision Making Module makes the appropriate API call to backend systems based on contextual information extracted by NLU module for further processing;
     - The processed output from decision-making system feeds back into Natural Language Understanding submodule that formulates a coherent response, which then passes through User Interface components before being delivered as an audible or visible message to the user. 

5. Security and Privacy Considerations: Ensure compliance with regulations like GDPR by incorporating privacy-enhancing technologies such as homomorphic encryption for sensitive data at rest, end-to-end (E2EE) encrypted channels using protocols like Signal Protocol etc.; Incorporate access control mechanisms to manage user permissions and restrict unauthorized access; 
     - Implement secure authentication/authorization system with the use of multi-factor verification methods such as OAuth or biometrics. Use data anonymization techniques for personal information used in machine learning algorithms that require sensitive inputs without directly accessing personally identifiable information (PII). Maintain a logging mechanism to monitor user activity and track possible security threats;

6. Scalability: Plan scalable system architecture using microservices approach where each module acts as an independent service communicating with other services via well-defined APIs ensuring that the entire AI Assistant can grow into different languages, industries or markets without significant alterations to existing codebase;  Use containerization and orchestration tools like Docker & Kubernetes for smooth deployment of microservices across multiple servers/data centers.

7. Maintainability: Ensure system modularity by using a well-defined API contract between different modules allowing easy modification or replacement without affecting overall functionality; Establish regular code reviews, testing procedures and documentation standards to maintain high quality of source codes throughout the entire development lifecycle from planning stages till after deployment/maintenance.

8. Conclusion: Summarize key aspects covered in this document regarding modular AI assistant system design including main components with subsystems or modules that interact seamlessly, communication protocol and data flow diagrams to show how information travels between different parts of the architecture; highlight security and privacy considerations for user protection during interactions as well as scalability & maintainability aspects discussed previously.

9. References: Cite references used throughout this document based on industry standards or academic sources that were considered relevant while designing a modular AI assistant system high-level viewpoint including any third party libraries, APIs and frameworks utilized in development process to achieve desired results effectively within the set constraints of time & budget allocation;

10. Appendix: Provide additional diagrams or charts (e.g., entity-relationship diagram for database schema design) illustrating system structure beyond main components as discussed earlier along with any relevant technical specifications, code samples etc.; also include documentation templates and examples of how data is collected/handled in various stages throughout the process such as input intents extraction from natural language queries by NLU module before passing onto decision making sub-module for further processing.
